 "title": "Enlarged lymph node: after history and exam, a benign self-limited cause is treated or explained, autoimmune or serious infection gets specific tests, red flags go to bloods, imaging and excisional biopsy, and unexplained nodes are worked up if generalized or watched for a month if regional; for a regional node the site points to the cause",
